# Course Forge — build-time config for `docker compose`
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# This file is ONLY for the Docker deployment. Docker Compose automatically
# reads a `.env` sitting next to compose.yaml and uses it to fill in the
# ${...} placeholders there.
#
# It is NOT the application's config. Azure keys, the YouTube key, JWT_SECRET,
# SMTP and everything else the backend reads live in backend/.env — see
# backend/.env.example. compose.yaml loads that file into the api container
# separately.
#
# Both files are gitignored.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Google Sign-In client ID (OPTIONAL)
#
# The public OAuth client ID — not a secret, and not the client secret. Leave it
# empty and the "Sign in with Google" button simply doesn't render; email and
# username sign-in keep working.
#
# Two things to get right when deploying:
#   1. Set the SAME value as GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID in backend/.env. The frontend uses
#      it to render the button, the backend to verify the token Google returns.
#   2. Add your production URL (https://your.domain) to the client's "Authorized
#      JavaScript origins" in Google Cloud Console. On an unlisted origin,
#      Google sign-in fails SILENTLY — check this before debugging anything else.
#
# Vite inlines this at BUILD time, so changing it needs:
#   docker compose up -d --build web
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=

# iOS app only: the iOS OAuth client ID (Google Cloud Console → Credentials →
# iOS, bundle ID ai.courseforgeapp.app). The website ignores it; the app hides
# its Google button while it's empty. Also a build-time value.
VITE_GOOGLE_IOS_CLIENT_ID=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Google Drive import on the Career Boost resume dialog (website only).
# Needs VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID above plus, in the SAME Cloud project:
#   1. Enable "Google Picker API" and "Google Drive API" (APIs & Services → Library)
#   2. Credentials → Create API key, restrict it to the Picker API and to
#      HTTP referrers http://localhost:5173/* and https://your.domain/*
#   3. OAuth consent screen → Data access → add the .../auth/drive.file scope
#      (non-sensitive — the app only sees the one file the user picks)
#   4. VITE_GOOGLE_APP_ID is the project NUMBER from the Cloud console dashboard
# Both are public values. Leave either empty and the Drive button stays hidden.
# Build-time, like the client ID.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
VITE_GOOGLE_API_KEY=
VITE_GOOGLE_APP_ID=
